# Vulnerabilities `make scan-image-cpu` / `publish-image-cpu` accept on purpose.
#
# Same format and rules as images/gpu/scan-ignore: one advisory id per line, `#` starts a
# comment, every entry names the issue that removes it and an expiry date. No `pkg:` scope
# field: trivy reads this file in its plain format and would ignore it (see images/gpu).

# wandb-core, the Go binary inside the wandb 0.31.0 wheel (Go stdlib 1.27.2, x/net 0.61.0);
# trivy reports these, osv-scanner cannot see inside the binary. wandb is tracking-only and
# defaults off in every step, so the binary does not run unless a recipe turns tracking on.
# No wandb release bundles the fixed Go deps yet (as of 2026-11-20); the raise is
# #752 (this image has no vllm, so #676 does not touch it).
# Ids from trivy's report on the c1069dfd image. Until 2027-05-31.
CVE-2026-78661
CVE-2026-111943
# GO-2026-5932: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained (Go vuln DB; no CVE alias,
# no severity score, so trivy reports it as UNKNOWN; the "fix" is a deprecation
# pseudo-version of x/crypto). Found once the trivy gate also checked UNKNOWN. Whether
# wandb-core imports openpgp at all is not verified; accepted on the same grounds as the
# ids above, and removed by the same raise (#752). Until 2027-05-31.
GO-2026-5932
